# Phase 3 – Course Database Specification & Authoring Kit

This phase defines the database standards for offline-first course packages, the packaging folder structure, asset encryption guidelines, local schema migration strategies, and provides a Course Authoring Kit tool along with a complete sample course.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The course packages (`<course_id>.db`) are designed as read-only SQLite databases downloaded by the mobile application. All user progress (box levels, review dates, favorites) is stored separately in the app's central `app_local.db` database using a composite key: `(course_id, card_number)`. This ensures content updates can be downloaded and replaced seamlessly without affecting the user's progress.

> [!NOTE]
> Media files (images and audio) inside the package will be encrypted using **AES-256-CBC** on the content server / authoring tool. The mobile client will decrypt them dynamically in RAM. The decryption keys will be distributed by the backend during authentication.

## Open Questions

None at this time. The architecture integrates with the already approved database design and security document from Phase 1 and Phase 2.

